# =============================================================================
# What does NOT belong in the repository.
#
# The working folder is ~726 MB; this brings the tracked tree to roughly 15 MB.
# The rule applied throughout: exclude anything that is (a) someone else's to
# distribute, or (b) regenerable from tracked code plus public archives. Keep
# everything a reader needs to understand and check the results.
# =============================================================================

# --- Third-party data: 371 MB, not ours to redistribute ----------------------
# The mentor's data pack. Obtain it separately; every script reads it read-only
# through data_manifest.py and none of them modify it.
exoplanet_research_data/

# --- Regenerable build products: 153 MB, 15,317 files ------------------------
# One .npz per KOI/TOI (global + local view). Rebuild with, e.g.:
#   python preprocessing_pipeline.py build-split train --discard-raw --s3
#   python preprocessing_pipeline.py build-split train --mission TESS --discard-raw --s3
# progress.jsonl is the per-star checkpoint and is also regenerable, but it is
# what makes a build resumable - keep a copy outside the repo before deleting.
detection_views/

# --- Regenerable model cache: 116 MB -----------------------------------------
# Consolidated view stacks. cnn_lstm.py rebuilds any of these automatically when
# the number of source .npz files changes.
stage_a_transit_model/cache/

# --- Sweep checkpoints -------------------------------------------------------
# 26 .pt files, ~5 MB. The two FINAL models are kept (negated below) so results
# can be reproduced without re-running the whole sweep; the 20+ exploratory runs
# are not, since sweep.py regenerates them.
stage_a_transit_model/runs/*/best.pt
!stage_a_transit_model/runs/bn_aug_sched/best.pt
!stage_a_transit_model/runs/tess_bn_aug_sched/best.pt

# --- Large derived data ------------------------------------------------------
# 20 MB PyATMOS roll-up, rebuilt by the Stage 2 habitability scripts.
datasets/pyatmos_final.csv

# --- Duplicated split files --------------------------------------------------
# splits/<mission>/{train,val,test}.csv are byte-equivalent to the rows the master
# catalogue already carries under its `split` column - verified identical columns,
# counts and star->KOI mapping. 21.7 MB of pure duplication. Ignored here as well as
# listed by tools/clean_workspace.py, so they cannot be committed by accident even
# if they are still on disk.
splits/kepler/
splits/tess/
splits/k2/

# --- Run noise ---------------------------------------------------------------
stdout_*.txt
stderr_*.txt
tess_chain.log
build_pid.txt
stage_a_transit_model/logs/
_cleanup_backup_*/

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Editors / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# =============================================================================
# Deliberately TRACKED, despite being outputs:
#   eda/*.md              the written results
#   eda/*.png             the figures those results refer to
#   outputs/**            small result tables (Stage B, Stage C, labels)
#   stage_a_transit_model/runs/**/report.json, *.csv, final_eval.json
#   detection_views_sample/  252 real views, so the code runs after a plain clone
#   run_log.txt           the project's running record of decisions and findings
#   splits/*.csv          the split definitions - without these no result is
#                         reproducible, because train/val/test membership is read
#                         from them and never recomputed. ~43 MB; see README for
#                         how to slim them if the repo needs to be smaller.
# =============================================================================

# --- release bundles (uploaded as Release assets, never committed) ------------
# The combined archive, the per-split archives that package_release.py --per-split
# writes, and the staging files both use. The staging patterns matter: an
# interrupted run leaves a ~150 MB file behind, and without them `git add -A`
# would commit it into history permanently.
detection_views_full.zip
detection_views_full.tmp
release_assets/
*.zip.part
